  "id": "Compound::DB00340 - Gene::1132",
  "verbalization": "Metixene is shown to bind to multiple acetylcholine receptor subunits—Chrm1, Chrm2, and Chrm3—each of which participates in the G-protein coupled acetylcholine receptor activity. This pathway leads to a direct interaction with Chrm4, suggesting that Metixene may modulate the function of the cholinergic receptor system. The high scores in the paths indicate a strong, consistent interaction across different receptor subunits, suggesting that Metixene may act as a broad-acting agonist or modulator of cholinergic signaling. The mechanism appears to involve binding to the receptor subunit, which then activates the G-protein cascade, ultimately influencing Chrm4's function. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Metixene and Chrm4, particularly through the G-protein-coupled acetylcholine receptor pathway, and the consistent scores across different paths suggest a robust and reliable relationship.",
